On 13 Apr 92 Josh writes

>Whenever I try to do this, I get the message "can't find configuration
>file."  I can run NetHack just fine when I'm outside the Windows environment.
>See, I just obtained a 386 and finally I'd like to be able to run the game
>from a window.

Windows 3.0 uses a one-line command for running applications, meaning that
the default directory will *not* be the one containing the nethack overlay
files. The simplest workaround is to write a small batch file something like

CD \GAMES\NETHACK
NETHACK

call it NH.BAT and run it when you want to play the game. (To avoid problems
don't call the batch file NETHACK.BAT!). I haven't tried this out but am
fairly confident it will work.

